-- title:
--   Drinfeld chart for the completed stalk, with level and inertia riders
-- statement:
--   Numerical data: a prime $q\ge 5$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$.
--
--   Coefficients: a field $L$ of characteristic zero, an element $\zeta\in L$ which is a primitive $q$-th root of unity, an element $\xi\in L$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and the hypothesis `hι` that some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$.
--
--   Function field: an intermediate field $K$ of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with `hK` asserting that $K$ is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the field of $q$-expansions of modular functions of level $\Gamma_H$ for $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   Base ring: a discrete valuation domain $A$ with a fraction-field structure $A\subseteq L$, with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$; an element $j\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$), with $j\neq 0$; a uniformiser $\varpi$, so $\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$; and an element $t\in A$ with $t^{q-1}=q\,w$ for some unit $w$ (`ht`).
--
--   The point: write $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model, the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra `chartAlgFin` of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. Given is a point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$, the element $\varpi_z$ defined in `hϖz` as the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak X$ obtained from $\varpi$ along the structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, with `hz` asserting $\varpi_z\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}}$; a point $y$ of `XFin = Spec (chartAlgFin A ↥K j)` with `ιFin` carrying $y$ to $z$; and the supersingularity hypothesis `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no non-zero affine point killed by $q$.
--
--   Conclusion. There exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$ (a domain, a discrete valuation ring, and $\mathfrak m_W$-adically complete), a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u$ and $v$ units, such that $f$ agrees with [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $=X_0X_1^{\,q}-X_0^{\,q}X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, together with a ring isomorphism
--   $$e:\ \widehat{\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}}\ \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\ S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma t)\,v-f\,u\big),$$
--   the completion being the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion `AdicCompletion` of the stalk at $z$ with respect to its maximal ideal. Write `toC` for the canonical map from the stalk to its completion, `mkS` for the quotient map onto $S$, and `germY` for the canonical ring homomorphism from `chartAlgFin` into the stalk at $z$ (the germ at $z$ of a chart function, via the identification of the sections of $\mathfrak X$ over the open image of `ιFin` with `chartAlgFin`). These data satisfy three assertions.
--
--   (1) Constants. For every $a\in A$, $e$ carries the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of the global section attached to $a$ by `toBase` to the class of the constant $C(\sigma a)$.
--
--   (2) Level equivariance. For every $\gamma\in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is: for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f_1,g_1$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H(N_0,H)$ regarded inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$, all integral power series realising their $q$-expansions, with the series attached to $g_1$ non-zero, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the ratio of those two series, and every ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, one has $\iota$-coefficientwise image of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g_1\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$ equal to the $q$-expansion of $f_1\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\delta$ is the matrix with rows $(\delta_{00},\delta_{01}/m)$ and $(m\delta_{10},\delta_{11})$ — and for every proof that $\tau$ preserves `chartAlgFin`, if the induced endomorphism of `chartAlgFin` is trivial modulo the prime of $y$ (i.e. $\tau a-a$ lies in that prime for all chart elements $a$), then there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta\circ e\circ$`toC`$\circ$`germY` $=e\circ$`toC`$\circ$`germY`$\circ\tau$ on `chartAlgFin`; $\theta$ fixes the class of every constant $C(w)$, $w\in W$; for each index $jj$ the difference $\theta(\overline{X_{jj}})-\overline{\sum_{ii}C(M_{ii\,jj})X_{ii}}$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by $\overline{X_0},\overline{X_1}$; $c^{q+1}-1\in\mathfrak m_W$; $M_{ii\,jj}-c\,\gamma_{ii\,jj}\in\mathfrak m_W$ for all $ii,jj$ (the integer entries of $\gamma$ being cast into $W$); if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ then $c-1\in\mathfrak m_W$; and if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c-1\notin\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   (3) Inertia. For every $d\in(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, every ring automorphism $\sigma_L$ of $L$ and every ring automorphism $\sigma_A$ of $A$ such that $\sigma_A$ is compatible with $\sigma_L$ under $A\to L$ and $\sigma_A a-a\in\mathfrak m_A$ for all $a\in A$; for every $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$, every $\tilde\alpha\in A$ with $\sigma_A\pi=\tilde\alpha\pi$ and $\tilde\alpha^{\,q+1}-\bar d\in\mathfrak m_A$, where $\bar d$ is the image in $A$ of the natural-number representative of $d$; and for every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ acting coefficientwise through $\sigma_L$ on Laurent series — the following hold: $\tau$ preserves `chartAlgFin`; and for every proof of that preservation, the induced endomorphism of `chartAlgFin` is trivial modulo the prime of $y$, and there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, a ring automorphism $\sigma_W$ of $W$, an element $ct\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ such that: $\theta\circ e\circ$`toC`$\circ$`germY` $=e\circ$`toC`$\circ$`germY`$\circ\tau$ on `chartAlgFin`; $\sigma_W\circ\sigma=\sigma\circ\sigma_A$; $\sigma_W w-w\in\mathfrak m_W$ for all $w\in W$; $\theta$ acts on constants by $\sigma_W$, i.e. $\theta(\overline{C(w)})=\overline{C(\sigma_W w)}$; for each $jj$ the difference $\theta(\overline{X_{jj}})-\overline{\sum_{ii}C(M_{ii\,jj})X_{ii}}$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by $\overline{X_0},\overline{X_1}$; $ct-\sigma(\tilde\alpha^{\,q+1})\in\mathfrak m_W$; and for all $ii,jj$, $M_{ii\,jj}-ct\cdot e_{ii\,jj}\in\mathfrak m_W$, where $e$ is the matrix of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.diagOneElem q (d^q)⁻¹`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L233), namely $\mathrm{diag}(1,(d^q)^{-1})$ over $\mathbb Z/q$, its entries being read in $W$ through their natural-number representatives.
--
--   The same witnesses $W,\sigma,f,u,v,e$ serve all three assertions simultaneously.
--
--   This is the existence statement for the Drinfeld-style local model of the completed local ring of the two-chart integral model of the full-level modular curve at a supersingular point in characteristic $q$: the completed stalk is presented as $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma t\,v-f u)$ with $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$, and the presentation is chosen so that level automorphisms act with linear part a scalar multiple of $\bar\gamma$ and inertia acts semilinearly with linear part the tame character times $\mathrm{diag}(1,(d^q)^{-1})$. It feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.inertia_drinfeldChart_semilinear_linearPart_tameCharacter_diagOneElem_of_levelAut_linearPart_of_pow_eq_mul_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.inertia_drinfeldChart_semilinear_linearPart_tameCharacter_diagOneElem_of_levelAut_linearPart_of_pow_eq_mul_of_isAlgClosed), which extracts the tame-inertia law on the chart.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_levelAut_linearPart_inertia_of_mem_ssJSet_of_pow_eq_mul_of_isAlgClosed.lean

